    "title": "Tinderbox (5 SP)",
    "filename": "tinderbox.md",
    "content": "Tinderbox (5 SP) A Tinderbox is a small container holding flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil) used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a Candle, Lamp, Lantern, or Torch—or anything else with exposed fuel—takes a Bonus Action. Lighting any other fire takes 1 minute. Source: 5.2 SRD (D&D 2024) - Adventuring Gear",
    "contentHtml": "<h1 id=\"tinderbox5sp\">Tinderbox (5 SP)</h1>\n<p>A Tinderbox is a small container holding flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil) used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a Candle, Lamp, Lantern, or Torch—or anything else with exposed fuel—takes a Bonus Action. Lighting any other fire takes 1 minute.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><em>Source: 5.2 SRD (D&D 2024) - Adventuring Gear</em></p>",
    "url": "./html/tinderbox.html"
